  <region id="1" left="27" top="288" width="702" height="88" border="true" color="#000000" bgColor="#ffffc0" fontSize="10">
    <text lang="eng">
      <p>Admittances for the various elements are simply the inverse of their impedances.The expressions for inductors and capacitors should be expressed in terms of theoperating frequency for the circuit. Using the admittance matrix, it is possibleto find the resonnant frequency for the network, and the general frequency response.Admittance formulae for capacitors and inductors are shown below</p>
    </text>
  </region>
